const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/alternatives";
const title = "Shopify app alternatives: choose a migration job";
const desc = "Find the guide for your existing account, define the unmet requirement and compare staying, repairing or replacing against evidence you can collect.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8"><a class="link" href="/alternatives">Alternative guides</a> · <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Migration decisions</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Start with a documented selection job</h2>
<p>Write down the unmet requirement before choosing a replacement: a profile invoice to reconcile, a missing event, an unsafe queue, an unsupported channel or an operator task that takes too long. Compare repairing the existing setup with replacing only the failing part and replacing the wider platform. Rank candidates against your own required behavior, not a universal winner.</p>
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Selection job</th><th>Evidence to gather</th><th>Decision exercise</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Explain a profile bill</td><td>Billable status, imports, duplicates, suppression treatment and dated contract.</td><td>Price the same eligible audience after correcting data hygiene.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Replace a workflow</td><td>Trigger, goal, delays, exclusions, catalog fields and event consumers.</td><td>Have the actual operator edit and pause one representative journey.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Change capture</td><td>Form locations, list destinations and channel permission fields.</td><td>Submit a new signup and an existing subscriber preference change.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repair channel economics</td><td>Reach, sends, destination charges and deduplicated contribution.</td><td>Compare the channel on equivalent eligibility and attribution windows.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recover from a retired product</td><td>Accessible archives, support correspondence and missing data.</td><td>Reconstruct ownership and permission before enabling a new sender.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Use a current native baseline</h2>
<p><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging">Shopify Messaging, formerly Shopify Email</a>, provides campaigns and email/SMS automations in Shopify. Check availability and requirements in your account. Demonstrate the missing journey against that baseline before paying for another platform; native does not mean it must be outgrown.</p>
<p><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo’s current notice</a> says its SMS application is decommissioned and dashboard/background services are inactive. <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo’s migration announcement</a> scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Yotpo Email &amp; SMS and SMSBump links below serve historical continuity work, not new procurement. Firepush’s <a class="link" href="https://getfirepush.com/web-push-apps-compared/">current comparison page</a> describes web push only; old email/SMS material does not establish current channel availability. Supplier scope checked November 25, 2026.</p>
<h2>Find the guide for the account you already have</h2><p>These links preserve existing guide routes. Inclusion is navigation, not a current product recommendation or a quality endorsement of every linked page.</p><h3>Lifecycle and customer-data accounts</h3><ul>
